## Summary

I injected `data-semtag-*` hints across every screen of this app (CompetencyHub — a job-competency modeling tool with a search screen and a model-detail screen reached via client-side state, plus a 404 page). No shared UI primitive needed prop-widening — all shadcn/Radix components already spread `...props` onto their root DOM node.

**Screens/components annotated:**
- `pages/Index.tsx` — persistent header nav ("Models" → navigation back to search)
- `pages/NotFound.tsx` — "Return to Home" link
- `components/competency/JobSearch.tsx` — search input, department select (with `data-semtag-options` + per-option `role="option"`), and the job-results grid as a folded `collection` (`jobs.search.results.item.<model.id>`)
- `components/competency/ModelDetailView.tsx` — back navigation, title/department observables, export/share/save actions
- `components/competency/MetricsPanel.tsx` — region wrapper + 4 metric observables + gap/healthy alert observables
- `components/competency/CompetencyGraph.tsx` + `CompetencyNode.tsx` — the ReactFlow canvas as a `collection` (`model.graph`), with each node folded as `model.graph.item.<competencyId>` exposing its enable toggle, weight slider, discrete level-picker (5 explicit `set-level-N` actions, since it's not a real range input), and category/critical/gap observables
- `components/competency/SimulationPanel.tsx` — region, scenario tab actions, per-category level/weight sliders, run/reset actions
- `components/competency/TemplateLibrary.tsx` — region, save-as-template action, and the template list folded as `model.templates.list.item.<templateId>`

**Id namespaces:** `header.*`, `jobs.search.*`, `model.detail.*`, `model.metrics.*`, `model.graph.*`, `model.simulation.*`, `model.templates.*`, `notfound.*`. All verified unique at runtime (only one job model's graph/detail view is ever mounted at a time; only one `TabsContent`/Radix tab panel is mounted at a time; model and competency ids are unique in the data file).

**Collections I could not cleanly fold as pure "select" or "toggle":** the level-picker in each graph node is implemented as 5 plain buttons rather than a real slider/select, so I modeled it as 5 individually addressable actions (`.level.1`…`.level.5`) plus a `.level` observable for the current label — the closed vocabulary has no "button-group" role, and this was the most honest fit.

**Left unhinted (deliberately):** decorative header "Analytics" link and footer links (all `href="#"`, no real destination or handler), the static hero stat cards, per-item keyword badges, and category/connection-count badges in job/template cards — none of these are things an agent needs to navigate to, act on, or uniquely read.

**Validation:** `validate-semtags.mjs` reports 42 hinted elements, 0 errors, 0 warnings. `tsc --noEmit`, `vite build`, and `vitest run` all pass; `eslint` shows only pre-existing errors/warnings in files I never touched (`command.tsx`, `textarea.tsx`, `tailwind.config.ts`, etc.).

One note for the record: the SimulationPanel's `model.simulation.content`/`.run`/`.reset` ids are written once in JSX inside a `.map()` over 3 scenarios but Radix `Tabs` only mounts the active `TabsContent`, so there's no runtime collision — the linter's static duplicate-id check doesn't (and can't) see this, but it's a false-positive risk worth knowing about if the scenario list ever changes to force-mount all tabs.

